  "id": "DrugBank_DB00960 - MONDO_5044",
  "verbalization": "Pindolol, a beta-blocker, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hypertensive Disorder through a series of mechanistic links. The evidence suggests that Pindolol may contribute to the development of Hypertensive Disorder via the induction of Second Degree Atrioventricular Block, a side effect that is also observed in other agents like Losartan and Propranolol. This indicates a potential role of Pindolol in the pathophysiology of hypertension, possibly through its effects on cardiac conduction and blood pressure regulation. The presence of a synergistic interaction with Phalaris Minor Pollen, which leads to Labetalol, further suggests that Pindolol may interact with other compounds to influence blood pressure, though the direct mechanism of this interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of hypertension and the potential for Pindolol to be involved in its development through multiple routes, though the exact mechanisms require further investigation.",
